    Central package management is enabled before dependencies are admitted. This bootstrap intentionally
    uses only framework/BCL references, so there is no NuGet package graph to lock yet. Add each external
    dependency here only after its license, security, and architectural role are reviewed; that task must
    also introduce and commit the applicable NuGet lock file for executable roots.

    Blocker/evidence note (2026-08-07): SQLite admission is blocked pending the SP02-T01 dependency-
    admission proof. The Microsoft.Data.Sqlite meta-package was rejected for the M1 registry/lock port
    because its transitive SQLitePCLRaw.lib.e_sqlite3 <= 2.1.11 carries the known high-severity
    CVE-2025-6965 (SQLite < 3.50.2, GHSA-2m69-gcr7-jv3q) with no patched release. The candidate combination
    (Microsoft.Data.Sqlite.Core 10.0.10, MIT; plus SQLitePCLRaw.bundle_e_sqlite3 3.0.5, Apache-2.0,
    referenced directly and centrally versioned) is a candidate, not an accepted decision: it passes only
    after the exhaustive SP02-T01 proof in dependency-securityfork-resolution.md succeeds. No dependency-
    free or other fallback persistence mechanism substitutes for the locked SQLite technology.
  -->
